# Copy to .env and fill in. Both paths read this same file: `docker compose` interpolates it
# into docker-compose.yaml, and `npm run dev` has Next load it directly, so dev and the
# container cannot drift apart. .env is gitignored; this example is not.

# REQUIRED. The Kokoro server this app synthesises through: any instance of ../server.
# There is no default anywhere in the source, on purpose. A wrong guess would send a
# streamer's chat to somebody else's box, so leaving this unset fails loudly instead:
# `docker compose up` refuses to start, and `npm run dev` answers /api/tts/* with a 500
# whose detail names this variable.
#
# Include the /tts prefix if you serve the API under one, as the reference deployment does.
# Server-side only: it is deliberately not NEXT_PUBLIC_*, so it never reaches the browser.
TTS_BASE_URL=https://tts.example.com/tts

# REQUIRED. The Twitch application this signs in as — the Client ID from your app in
# https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps. No default anywhere in the source: which app issues the
# token decides which redirect URLs are registered and who can revoke it, and a fallback onto
# someone else's app ID would only show up as a `redirect_mismatch` later, so unset fails
# loudly instead. `docker compose up --build` refuses to build, and `npm run dev` fails the
# sign-in with a message naming this variable.
#
# Public by design: the implicit flow puts it in the authorize URL and there is no client
# secret, which is why it is NEXT_PUBLIC_* and reaches the browser. That makes it BUILD-time
# like NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH — a change needs `docker compose up -d --build`, not a restart.
#
# Register every URL the app is served from, each ending in /auth/callback, as an OAuth
# Redirect URL on that app. Twitch compares redirect_uri as a raw string, so the base path is
# part of it. See README, "Before it will sign in: Twitch app setup".
NEXT_PUBLIC_TWITCH_CLIENT_ID=your-twitch-client-id

# OPTIONAL, defaults to /moneytts. The subpath the app is served under, which Next owns via
# `basePath`. Baked in at BUILD time, so changing it needs `docker compose up -d --build`,
# not a restart, and it has to match the location block in your reverse proxy. Set it to an
# empty value to serve the app from the root of its own hostname.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/moneytts
